# DTF tier manifest: virtual-member-gates-1120
#   (artifact-keeper#5146, #5147, #5150, #5151; all fixed on main for 1.12.0,
#   none on the 1.11.x line)
# Profile-set: filesystem + a run-time-filled upstream (upstreams.mock-files:
# a stdlib-python server on 172.16.<slot>.76 whose files the oracle writes over
# a control API). The mock stands in for an OCI registry (static /v2/ paths),
# two npm registries and three PyPI indexes, each under its own path prefix.
# Proxy scan verdicts come from the backend image's bundled Grype (a clean
# scan of a one-layer image); the oracle then re-grades that verdict to a
# medium-severity `vulnerable` row, as #5146 asks ("seed that verdict instead
# of assuming today's findings").
#
# THE BUGS
# #5146  OCI: adding an EMPTY hosted member to a Docker virtual made the blob
#        gate block-on-any, so the config and layer of a remote image whose
#        vulnerable verdict is below the severity threshold answered 403
#        "blob belongs to an image blocked by scan policy", while its manifest
#        served and a remote-only virtual served everything.
# #5147  NuGet: a package whose stored `artifacts.name`/`path` is mixed-case
#        (rows written by the Artifactory importer) downloaded from its hosted
#        repository but 404'd through a virtual over it.
# #5150  Age gate: in an npm or PyPI virtual, a gated Remote member whose
#        upstream does not host the package answered 451 (no publish time =
#        too young) and ended the request, so the member that hosts an old
#        version was never asked.
# #5151  PyPI age gate: with an upstream that has only the PEP 503 simple
#        index (no Warehouse JSON API) every version was blocked, even at
#        min_age_days = 0; the simple index's `data-upload-time` was ignored.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      RED on ak 1.11.13, GREEN on main:
#              #5146 virtual [empty hosted, Remote] serves the config and
#                    layer blobs of the below-threshold image (200, not 403);
#              #5147 virtual [hosted] downloads the mixed-case stored
#                    .nupkg by the lowercase and the mixed-case URL;
#              #5150 npm virtual [gated, not hosting; gated, hosting] and
#                    PyPI virtual [gated, not hosting; gated, hosting] serve
#                    the old version (200, not 451) and write no review on the
#                    member that does not host it;
#              #5151 simple-index-only PyPI Remote: min_age_days 0 serves an
#                    undated file, min_age_days 7 serves a file whose
#                    data-upload-time is 2020.
#   (CONTROL)  must hold on BOTH images: a remote-only Docker virtual serves
#              manifest, config and layer; the manifest through the virtual
#              with the empty hosted member serves; direct hosted NuGet
#              downloads (both spellings) serve; a natively pushed package
#              serves through the virtual; each hosting npm / PyPI member
#              serves the old version directly; a file dated today is still
#              451 at min_age_days 7 on the simple-index-only Remote.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~100 requests back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock upstream is on a private subnet.
COVERS="5146 5147 5150 5151"
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-files"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
